PROJECT 1: TRANSACTION DATA PIPELINE
Real-Life Context
A company receives a daily text file containing transaction records.
Some records are invalid.
The company wants a small software system that can:
•	read the transaction file
•	validate the records
•	separate clean and invalid data
•	generate a business report
This project simulates a real Data Engineering + Data Analysis task.
________________________________________
Input File
Create a file named transactions.txt
Example content:
user_id,amount,category
U1,100,food
U2,-50,shopping
U3,200,travel
U4,abc,food
U5,300,shopping
U6,120,food
U7,,travel
U8,450,electronics
________________________________________
Problem Statement
Write a Python program using only file handling that processes the above transaction file and produces clean data, error logs, and a final report.
________________________________________
Step-by-Step Tasks
Step 1: Read the file
Read the transactions.txt file line by line.
Requirements:
•	Use with open(...)
•	Do not use readlines()
•	Process one line at a time
________________________________________
Step 2: Validate each row
For each row, validate the following:
•	row must contain exactly 3 fields
•	amount must not be empty
•	amount must be numeric
•	amount must not be negative
If any validation fails, the row should be treated as invalid.
________________________________________
Step 3: Create clean output
Write all valid rows into a file named clean.txt
Format:
•	preserve the same fields
•	write one valid record per line
________________________________________
Step 4: Create error log
Write all invalid rows into a file named error.log
Each error entry must include:
•	the original row
•	the reason for failure
Examples:
U2,-50,shopping -> Negative amount
U4,abc,food -> Non-numeric amount
U7,,travel -> Missing amount
Requirements:
•	log errors in real time
•	use flush() after writing each error
________________________________________
Step 5: Generate analytics report
Create a file named report.txt
The report must contain:
•	Total Records
•	Valid Records
•	Invalid Records
•	Total Revenue
•	Category-wise Revenue
Example format:
Total Records: 8
Valid Records: 5
Invalid Records: 3
Total Revenue: 1170.0

Category-wise Revenue:
food: 220.0
travel: 200.0
shopping: 300.0
electronics: 450.0
________________________________________
Step 6: Use at least one file positioning method
In your program, use either:
•	tell()
•	seek()
This is to demonstrate cursor awareness in file handling.
________________________________________
Expected Output Files
After program execution, these files must exist:
•	clean.txt
•	error.log
•	report.txt



